       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 4000 mg per dose is 10 times a standard 400 mg dose. 16,000 mg/day is well into the range where ibuprofen toxicity is expected, and I know of no indication that calls for it. Entering it would likely lead to serious harm, and a nurse or pharmacy might not catch it before the first dose.\n\nHere is what I can do right now:\n\n- Enter a standard dose, such as 400 mg or 800 mg PO, at the frequency you choose.\n- Enter a different regimen if you're aiming for a particular effect, such as maximal anti-inflammatory dosing at 800 mg PO three times daily.\n- Add a note to an order, for example \"take with food\" or \"reassess in 48 hours.\"\n\nIf you believe this dose is clinically necessary, for example in a protocol I'm not aware of, please enter it directly. That way pharmacy can review it and the order will go through their high-dose verification."
      }
